# PXA preset -- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-class MoE (qwen35moe, PXQN4 file with its MTP head) on TWO Tesla P100 16 GB (sm_60), layer split
#
# This is what a bare launch of that cell now does by itself (registry pick PXA_AUTO_P60 + the chain row PXA_SPEC_AUTO_MOE_MTP): the file exists so an
# older binary, a PXA_ENHANCE=0 seat or a container can load the same switches by hand (docker --env-file, or `set -a; . file`).
#
# Eleven levers that are OFF in the engine: the persistent single-token layer halves (PXA_P60_MEGA, and for the speculative verify the 2..6-token PXQN4 MoE half
# PXA_P60_MEGA_PXQN_T), the verify-width GEMVs (PXA_KQMMV_VW, PXA_PXQN_VW, PXA_P60_PRE_VW) and the decode-width PXQN4 kernels around the delta-net conv cluster.
# Measured 2026-10-16 (patched binary, greedy 256, 6 prompts per class, plain boot 125 t/s with the stack on the same box and client):
#   bare launch before (n-gram chain, no stack)      74 t/s on every class
#   stack + MTP n_max 3 p_min 0.85 (the default row)  138 / 151 / 130 t/s prose / code / chat (+10 / +21 / +3.5% over plain WITH the stack), sampled 127 / 149 / 123
#   stack + MTP n_max 1 p_min 0 (conservative row)    134 / 148 / 132 t/s
# Not bit-identical to the stack off at decode / verify widths, and correct: det 12/12 (short, 8k prose, 8k code), needle 28k x2, PPL ratio 1.0012 +- 0.0016, decode KLD vs off
# 2.5e-3 (the engine's own width noise 1.8e-3). Off switch of the registry pick: PXA_AUTO_P60=0.
#
# Server arguments of the measurement:
#   llama-server -m <Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-PXQN4>.gguf -ngl 99 -sm layer -fa on -c 32768 -b 8192 -ub 256 -np 1 -t 8 --jinja --cache-ram 0 \
#     --spec-type mtp:n_max=3,p_min=0.85
PXA_P60_MEGA=1
PXA_P60_MEGA_PXQN_T=1
PXA_KQMMV_VW=1
PXA_PXQN_VW=1
PXA_P60_PRE_VW=1
PXA_PXQN_RBP=1
PXA_PXQN_RMS_RHT_GB=1
PXA_ARGMAX_VAL_MB=1
PXA_DN_CONVFUSE=1
PXA_FA_GQA_PACK=0
PXA_PXQN_QPN=1
